From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sysretq0 <sysretq0@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 04:12:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] media: mediatek: jpeg: Set 34-bit DMA mask when IOMMU-mapped on 64-bit DMA

On MediaTek 34-bit M4U platforms (such as MT6789 and MT8186), LARB7
(VENC/JPGENC) is assigned to IOMMU Region 1 (4 GiB..8 GiB IOVA), where
SMI LARB7 prepends bank bit 32 to the 32-bit addresses programmed into
the JPEG encoder registers. Ensure an IOMMU-mapped JPEG device advertises
a 34-bit DMA mask on 64-bit DMA builds so iommu-dma can allocate IOVAs in
Region 1 without failing against the default 32-bit DMA mask.

Signed-off-by: sysretq0 <sysretq0@proton.me>
---
 drivers/media/platform/mediatek/jpeg/mtk_jpeg_core.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/mediatek/jpeg/mtk_jpeg_core.c b/drivers/media/platform/mediatek/jpeg/mtk_jpeg_core.c
--- a/drivers/media/platform/mediatek/jpeg/mtk_jpeg_core.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/mediatek/jpeg/mtk_jpeg_core.c
@@ -12,6 +12,7 @@
 #include <linux/clk.h>
 #include <linux/err.h>
 #include <linux/interrupt.h>
+#include <linux/iommu.h>
 #include <linux/io.h>
 #include <linux/kernel.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
@@ -1307,6 +1308,16 @@ static int mtk_jpeg_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 	platform_set_drvdata(pdev, jpeg);
 
+	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_ARCH_DMA_ADDR_T_64BIT) &&
+	    device_iommu_mapped(&pdev->dev)) {
+		ret = dma_set_mask_and_coherent(&pdev->dev, DMA_BIT_MASK(34));
+		if (ret) {
+			dev_err(&pdev->dev,
+				"Failed to set 34-bit DMA mask: %d\n", ret);
+			return ret;
+		}
+	}
+
 	ret = devm_of_platform_populate(&pdev->dev);
 	if (ret) {
 		v4l2_err(&jpeg->v4l2_dev, "Master of platform populate failed.");
-- 
